// EXPECT: PASS
// Phase 2 slice 2 OVER-REJECTION GUARD — a guard that is constantly FALSE.
//
// The original collector skipped every guarded application on the stated reasoning that "charging
// a contract from a path that may not run would be an over-rejection". That reasoning is exactly
// right for THIS program: the branch is dead, `callee(-1)` never executes, and rejecting it would
// be a false rejection.
//
// The fix keeps that property by folding the guard: constant-false means the application is
// dropped. An earlier draft passed guards to the solver as assumptions instead, and this fixture
// is the one that caught it returning ANUBIS_ASSERTION_UNPROVEN — a fail-open traded for a false
// rejection, which is worse. It did not ship.
fn callee(x) requires(x >= 0) { return x; }

fn app(f) {
    if 1 == 2 { f(-1); }
}

fn main() { app(callee); }
